From 98db9a2ada4cc353e50dc0bec5bebc0c293263ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:37:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sim): the posed fixture sweep reads a band as a
 flat-ended cylinder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The posed sweep of fixture laws (c2)/(d2) placed each band of a leaning
stack as a capsule, whose caps reach a whole band radius past each end:
a holder standing 0.5 mm over a clamp was convicted at any lean. A box
the capsule reaches is now read a second time against the band as the
cylinder it is - the interval's tip chord swept exactly, the cylinder
about the midpoint pose, a ball for the swing and the arc bulge (the
fixture mesh law's enclosure) - and cleared only on a GJK proof of a
separating plane. The rim reaches R sin θ past the end plane, so the
verdict turns at the lean where the true band touches.

Both enclosures contain the swept band, so the law stays conservative;
non-finite input or an unfinished search is never a proof.

Fixes #1305

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
